{"version":1,"type":"session-summary","driving_event":"The rerun for PR #652 failed both smoke jobs: container-smoke reported Mosquitto connection refusal after daemon launch, and runner-smoke could not connect even after a readiness retry. CI showed the daemon was not accepting connections at all.","decision":"Run Mosquitto as a supervised foreground child in container-smoke and runner-smoke, capture its startup log, probe with a non-retained publish, and stop the child during cleanup. Preserve an already-running broker in runner-smoke.","impact":"Updated only the two smoke scripts. No application or dependency changes. Local shell syntax and harness checks pass; container execution in this development environment is blocked because /workspace/.build is not writable.","recurrence_control":"The smoke scripts now detect a dead broker process, print its startup log, and fail after a bounded readiness wait instead of racing daemonization or silently waiting for the runner.","rejected_alternatives":["Add another fixed delay while retaining daemon mode, because it cannot distinguish a slow startup from a broker that exited.","Change Runtime startup behavior without evidence that the runner was the source of the connection failure."],"sources":[]}
